From: Gauthier Piarrette <gauthierpiarrette@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Report the task footprint as the commit charge on macOS.

Adapted for CrossOver 26.3 from gauthierpiarrette/highball-engine
commit 500a0a7f1846900dfc576aebba3aa609420de846 (patch 0018). The code
is unchanged; only the hunk offsets differ. This is a downstream fix,
not a WineHQ backport or a game-specific change.

fill_vm_counters() reported PagefileUsage, which ProcessVmCounters
also returns as PrivateUsage, from the Mach task's virtual_size. That is
address space, and a 64-bit process under Rosetta maps tens of
gigabytes it never touches: a console program with a 9 MB working set
read 41,987 MB, unchanged after committing and touching 512 MB.
Windows reports the private commit charge. The Linux branch reports
RssAnon + VmSwap; the macOS counterpart is the task's phys_footprint
(dirty and compressed pages), which is also what Activity Monitor
shows. A program that budgets memory from this figure, or warns about
low memory from it, now sees memory it is actually charged for.

PeakPagefileUsage is the kernel's footprint high-water mark
(ledger_phys_footprint_peak, TASK_VM_INFO rev3) and at least the
current value; with an older answer it is the current value, as in the
Linux branch. VirtualSize and the working set are unchanged. When
TASK_VM_INFO is unavailable, the query fails or the answer predates
phys_footprint (rev1), the old values stay.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
index 1f550a60..c36891f4 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/process.c
@@ -1485,6 +1485,9 @@ void fill_vm_counters( VM_COUNTERS_EX *pvmi, int unix_pid )
 #if defined(MACH_TASK_BASIC_INFO)
     struct mach_task_basic_info info;
     mach_msg_type_number_t infoCount;
+#ifdef TASK_VM_INFO
+    task_vm_info_data_t vm_info;
+#endif
 
     if (unix_pid != -1) return; /* FIXME: Retrieve information for other processes. */
 
@@ -1496,6 +1499,22 @@ void fill_vm_counters( VM_COUNTERS_EX *pvmi, int unix_pid )
         pvmi->WorkingSetSize = info.resident_size;
         pvmi->PeakWorkingSetSize = info.resident_size_max;
     }
+#ifdef TASK_VM_INFO
+    /* The commit charge is memory the process is charged for, not address space. The footprint
+     * is what the kernel charges the task (dirty and compressed pages), the counterpart of the
+     * RssAnon + VmSwap sum used on Linux. */
+    infoCount = TASK_VM_INFO_COUNT;
+    if (task_info( mach_task_self(), TASK_VM_INFO, (task_info_t)&vm_info, &infoCount ) == KERN_SUCCESS &&
+        infoCount >= TASK_VM_INFO_REV1_COUNT)
+    {
+        pvmi->PagefileUsage = vm_info.phys_footprint;
+        pvmi->PeakPagefileUsage = pvmi->PagefileUsage;
+        /* The kernel keeps the footprint's high-water mark from rev3 on. */
+        if (infoCount >= TASK_VM_INFO_REV3_COUNT && vm_info.ledger_phys_footprint_peak > 0 &&
+            (ULONG64)vm_info.ledger_phys_footprint_peak > pvmi->PeakPagefileUsage)
+            pvmi->PeakPagefileUsage = vm_info.ledger_phys_footprint_peak;
+    }
+#endif
 #endif
 }
 
